 </p>
<div class="collapse" id="cook1">
  <div class="card card-body border-0">
   <p class="roboto" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">Bake in 400 F oven for 30 to 35 minutes or until internal temperature reaches 180 to 185 F</p>
  </div></div></div>
<div class="col-md-2">
<p data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#cook2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample" style="text-align:center" class="mb-5">
<img src="/images/content/external/PF-Wing-Landing-PG-Icon-Air-Fryer-80x80.png" alt="cooking chicken wings in air fryer"><br>
   <span class="roboto color-white" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">AIR FRYER &#9660;</span>

 </p>
<div class="collapse" id="cook2">
  <div class="card card-body border-0">
   <p class="roboto" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">Preheat air fryer to 400 F for 3 minutes then spray the basket with non-stick cooking spray. Place wings in a single layer in basket and spray with cooking spray. Set the timer for 20 minutes. After 10 minutes, flip wings and spray the other side. Air fry 10 minutes longer or until wings are golden brown, and internal temperature reaches 180 to 185 F.</p>
  </div></div></div>
<div class="col-md-2"><p data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#cook3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample" style="text-align:center" class="mb-5">
<img src="/images/content/external/PF-Wing-Landing-PG-Icon-Fryer-80x80.png" alt="how to deep fry chicken wings"><br>
   <span class="roboto color-white" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">DEEP FRYER &#9660;</span>

 </p>
<div class="collapse" id="cook3">
  <div class="card card-body border-0">
   <p class="roboto" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">Preheat deep fryer to 350 F. Fry wings in small batches, ensuring that they reach an internal temperature of 180 to 185 F.</p>
  </div></div></div>
<div class="col-md-2">
<p data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#cook4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample" style="text-align:center" class="mb-5">
<img src="/images/content/external/PF-Wing-Landing-PG-Icon-Grill-80x80.png" alt="how to grill chicken wings"><br>
   <span class="roboto color-white" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">GRILL &#9660;</span>

 </p>
<div class="collapse" id="cook4">
  <div class="card card-body border-0">
   <p class="roboto" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">Preheat grill to 400 F (medium-high heat). Cook wings for 12 to 15 minutes, flipping occasionally.</p>
  </div></div></div>
<div class="col-md-2">
<p data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#cook5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseExample" style="text-align:center" class="mb-5">
<img src="/images/content/external/PF-Wing-Landing-PG-Icon-Smoker-80x80.png" alt="how to smoke chicken wings"><br>
   <span class="roboto color-white" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">SMOKER &#9660;</span>

 </p>
<div class="collapse" id="cook5">
  <div class="card card-body border-0">
   <p class="roboto" style="font-size:20px; text-align:center">Preheat smoker to 225 F. Place wings on smoker rack and close lid. Smoke wings for two to three hours, or until they reach an internal temperature of 180 to 185 F.
